{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-romans-003",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 3,
  "title": "Romans 3",
  "display_title": "Romans 3",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "romans",
  "book": "Romans",
  "bookName": "Romans",
  "bookOrder": 45,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 3,
  "sortOrder": 45003,
  "verseCount": 31,
  "aliases": [
    "Rom",
    "Ro",
    "Rm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "What advantage then hath the Jew? or what profit is there of circumcision?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Much every way: chiefly, because that unto them were committed the oracles of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For what if some did not believe? shall their unbelief make the faith of God without effect?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "God forbid: yea, let God be true, but every man a liar; as it is written, That thou mightest be justified in thy sayings, and mightest overcome when thou art judged.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "But if our unrighteousness commend the righteousness of God, what shall we say? Is God unrighteous who taketh vengeance? (I speak as a man)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "God forbid: for then how shall God judge the world?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For if the truth of God hath more abounded through my lie unto his glory; why yet am I also judged as a sinner?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And not rather, (as we be slanderously reported, and as some affirm that we say,) Let us do evil, that good may come? whose damnation is just.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "What then? are we better than they? No, in no wise: for we have before proved both Jews and Gentiles, that they are all under sin;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "As it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "There is none that understandeth, there is none that seeketh after God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "They are all gone out of the way, they are together become unprofitable; there is none that doeth good, no, not one.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Their throat is an open sepulchre; with their tongues they have used deceit; the poison of asps is under their lips:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Whose mouth is full of cursing and bitterness:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Their feet are swift to shed blood:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Destruction and misery are in their ways:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And the way of peace have they not known:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "There is no fear of God before their eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Now we know that what things soever the law saith, it saith to them who are under the law: that every mouth may be stopped, and all the world may become guilty before God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Therefore by the deeds of the law there shall no flesh be justified in his sight: for by the law is the knowledge of sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "But now the righteousness of God without the law is manifested, being witnessed by the law and the prophets;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Even the righteousness of God which is by faith of Jesus Christ unto all and upon all them that believe: for there is no difference:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Whom God hath set forth to be a propitiation through faith in his blood, to declare his righteousness for the remission of sins that are past, through the forbearance of God;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "To declare, I say, at this time his righteousness: that he might be just, and the justifier of him which believeth in Jesus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Where is boasting then? It is excluded. By what law? of works? Nay: but by the law of faith.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Therefore we conclude that a man is justified by faith without the deeds of the law.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Is he the God of the Jews only? is he not also of the Gentiles? Yes, of the Gentiles also:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Seeing it is one God, which shall justify the circumcision by faith, and uncircumcision through faith.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:3:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Do we then make void the law through faith? God forbid: yea, we establish the law.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 3:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:3:31"
      }
    }
  ],
